**Version**: 1.1
**Status**: Draft — the model survives from the original as a set of rules rather than an essay. Ruled nodes carried: short-chain-is-legal, roles-global-and-stable, ring-is-device-owned, storage-is-a-new-service, delete-is-total, and rbac-eval-locus (David, 2026-08-18 — the device holds the full role table and gates locally). Slot-allocation corrected: the device owns physical allocation and the slot-to-person-character-rbac bridge; the service works in logical (person, ordinal) only and a slot never crosses the bus. Hashing removed throughout: identity is the set UUID, completeness is the entry count. Device-announcement shape, template-reference form, and the one-tier verification are proposed for the architect. [CXC-FPID-MATCH-CHAIN] carries its first REAL-hardware proof (2026-08-24): a GRANTED end-to-end run resolved all five hops on the physical part, with the caveat that this only became possible once [CXC-FPHAL-MATCH-USES-ENROLL-SENSOR] (C72) closed the mock/real-sensor fork that had masked it.
